--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- dynamic power cable shared by two floaters, both hang-offs moving, 36 s
-- A 360 m finite-EI array cable (the bare cable of the Lozon lazy-wave decks: D 0.16 m,
-- 36.7 kg/m, EI 1.99e4 N m^2) hangs in a free catenary between the hang-offs of two floaters
-- 300 m apart, 14 m below the surface, in 200 m of water: its lowest point is about 100 m deep,
-- clear of the seabed. Both ends are Coupled points, so End B moves as End A does: the motionFile
-- (data/shared/floaters_surge_heave_12s_dt0025.txt, written by generate_floater_motion.py) gives
-- each floater a 2 m surge and a 1.5 m heave at 12 s, floater 2 surging in antiphase so that
-- the span opens and closes by 4 m. Both hang-offs are clamped (Rigid) along their static
-- tangents; BendMom1N1 and BendMom1N73 are the hang-off moments, FairTen1 and AnchTen1 the two
-- hang-off tensions (End A and End B), L1N37pz the depth of the mid-span node.
